.TH READLINK 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
readlink \- print resolved symbolic links or canonical file names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readlink
[\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fIPATH\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the value of each symbolic link PATH. With \fB\-f\fR, resolves the entire path to an absolute, symlink-free form instead (like \fBrealpath\fR(1)).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-canonicalize
Canonicalize the whole path, following every symlink.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
